1
00:00:13,993 --> 00:00:17,038
OUR STICKY LOVE

2
00:00:50,822 --> 00:00:51,698
Kaito!

3
00:01:04,002 --> 00:01:04,836
Fuck.

4
00:01:09,174 --> 00:01:10,175
What the…

5
00:01:24,898 --> 00:01:25,857
GUJIN RICE TAFFY

6
00:01:43,625 --> 00:01:45,543
Honey! What are you doing here?

7
00:01:45,627 --> 00:01:48,338
Don't worry, honey. The ladies are here.

8
00:01:48,421 --> 00:01:49,505
So,

9
00:01:49,589 --> 00:01:53,176
all that turmoil that Tae-ha and Eun-sae
went through,

10
00:01:53,259 --> 00:01:55,428
and even Jeong-hwa's car accident…

11
00:01:55,511 --> 00:01:59,140
All along, that was all your doing?

12
00:01:59,224 --> 00:02:00,475
Hui-ja!

13
00:02:00,558 --> 00:02:03,895
-You don't seem to grasp the situation.
-Please don't.

14
00:02:03,978 --> 00:02:05,188
But these guys here--

15
00:02:05,271 --> 00:02:07,273
Hey, Geum-hyang!

16
00:02:07,357 --> 00:02:09,609
You ready?

17
00:02:09,692 --> 00:02:11,027
Aye.

18
00:02:12,528 --> 00:02:13,571
No problem.

19
00:02:15,907 --> 00:02:19,202
I was a shot put athlete
at Gujin Girls' Commercial High,

20
00:02:19,285 --> 00:02:22,080
you sons of guns!

21
00:02:31,589 --> 00:02:35,843
How dare you bastards
come barging into our village!

22
00:02:36,636 --> 00:02:38,429
Come at me!

23
00:02:41,891 --> 00:02:43,893
Anyone who messes with us
Taffy Village folk

24
00:02:43,977 --> 00:02:46,396
better be saying their prayers.

25
00:03:03,204 --> 00:03:04,205
Hold up.

26
00:03:04,289 --> 00:03:07,625
Song-wol is from North Korea, right?

27
00:03:07,709 --> 00:03:08,668
Yeah.

28
00:03:09,252 --> 00:03:11,629
I did hear that she used to be a soldier.

29
00:03:11,713 --> 00:03:15,174
Who needs tear gas when you can mix
vinegar with red pepper powder?

30
00:03:19,637 --> 00:03:20,555
Damn it!

31
00:03:20,638 --> 00:03:24,517
-You! How dare you hit him!
-No, that way!

32
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:26,686
I'll tear you limb from limb, you bastard!

33
00:03:27,437 --> 00:03:30,732
A son of a bitch like you
should have his guts ripped out

34
00:03:31,316 --> 00:03:34,694
and thrown into the mudflats,
but even the worms wouldn't eat you!

35
00:03:34,777 --> 00:03:38,614
How dare you touch my husband,
you absolute piece of filth!

36
00:03:38,698 --> 00:03:40,491
-Damn you! Die, you bastard!
-Stop her.

37
00:03:40,575 --> 00:03:41,743
-Honey.
-Stop her.

38
00:03:41,826 --> 00:03:44,495
Hey! He's my husband!

39
00:03:46,331 --> 00:03:49,167
Hang in there, okay? Just a little longer.

40
00:03:49,250 --> 00:03:50,460
Ma'am.

41
00:03:50,543 --> 00:03:52,295
-Hey, there you are.
-Yes.

42
00:03:52,378 --> 00:03:54,589
He's on our side,
but he's hurt pretty badly.

43
00:03:54,672 --> 00:03:56,674
You guys work at a hospital, so treat him.

44
00:03:56,758 --> 00:03:59,177
Are you… But ma'am,
we're a mental health clinic.

45
00:03:59,260 --> 00:04:00,219
Are you okay?

46
00:04:00,303 --> 00:04:01,888
-Yes, I'm okay.
-Where…

47
00:04:04,265 --> 00:04:05,850
Watch out!

48
00:04:13,983 --> 00:04:16,694
-An Gi-jun, are you okay?
-Yeah, I'm okay.

49
00:04:17,487 --> 00:04:18,363
I'll be okay,

50
00:04:19,030 --> 00:04:20,406
as long as

51
00:04:21,282 --> 00:04:22,325
you're okay.

52
00:04:47,683 --> 00:04:48,893
Pil-seung?

53
00:04:55,525 --> 00:04:57,110
-Why are you here?
-What?

54
00:04:57,193 --> 00:04:58,653
-What?
-It's dangerous!

55
00:04:58,736 --> 00:05:02,698
Why? What will I do with you?

56
00:05:13,334 --> 00:05:14,877
It's Eun-sae!

57
00:05:16,087 --> 00:05:17,839
Gang-rok, are you okay?

58
00:05:17,922 --> 00:05:18,756
Yes.

59
00:05:22,176 --> 00:05:23,511
What about Jang Tae-ha?

60
00:05:37,150 --> 00:05:37,984
Baek Sang-gil.

61
00:05:41,112 --> 00:05:42,822
I'll take whatever you give me.

62
00:05:45,241 --> 00:05:46,284
Just do it outside.

63
00:05:53,166 --> 00:05:55,585
Thought I wouldn't hear
the difference in your gloves?

64
00:05:57,086 --> 00:06:00,548
You think you can become
a national athlete with such dirty fists?

65
00:06:00,631 --> 00:06:03,176
Wouldn't it be good for you
if I make the national team?

66
00:06:05,261 --> 00:06:08,222
Taking you in as my disciple,
even for a short time,

67
00:06:08,306 --> 00:06:10,516
will have been
the most shameful thing in my life.

68
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:13,352
-Coach!
-From this moment on, I'm not your coach.

69
00:06:14,187 --> 00:06:16,522
I never taught you
to use your fists to harm others.

70
00:06:21,944 --> 00:06:23,279
Fuck this!

71
00:06:41,672 --> 00:06:44,008
Plaster in your gloves? Are you crazy?

72
00:06:44,091 --> 00:06:45,301
Why would you do that?

73
00:06:46,219 --> 00:06:48,971
-I needed to win to get paid.
-What?

74
00:06:49,055 --> 00:06:52,975
They said they bet big on me winning
and that it would all be mine if I won.

75
00:06:54,393 --> 00:06:58,231
How will we ever afford an oil boiler
or buy a Grandeur on an athlete's stipend?

76
00:06:58,314 --> 00:06:59,899
Who asked you for any of that?

77
00:07:00,775 --> 00:07:03,402
I liked boxing
because everyone was equal in the ring,

78
00:07:03,486 --> 00:07:06,614
fighting with nothing but their fists
regardless of status or wealth.

79
00:07:06,697 --> 00:07:10,910
And I liked you because of how you made it
this far with nothing but your fists.

80
00:07:16,541 --> 00:07:19,418
So go back to your coach and beg, okay?

81
00:07:21,254 --> 00:07:22,338
Forget it.

82
00:07:22,922 --> 00:07:24,298
I can just quit boxing.

83
00:07:24,382 --> 00:07:25,466
Baek Sang-gil.

84
00:07:26,592 --> 00:07:28,427
Are you going to keep disappointing me?

85
00:07:29,387 --> 00:07:31,514
Then you can just leave me too!

86
00:07:34,850 --> 00:07:36,018
What did you say?

87
00:07:37,061 --> 00:07:39,689
I won't spend my life always losing
like the rest of you.

88
00:07:59,166 --> 00:08:00,001
Hi.

89
00:08:02,878 --> 00:08:06,257
Since you lost the match today,
I can't give you the money.

90
00:08:06,340 --> 00:08:08,843
But I was thinking I'd give you
something else instead.

91
00:08:09,343 --> 00:08:11,762
Once you're banned
from the boxing association,

92
00:08:11,846 --> 00:08:13,347
you won't be able to box anymore.

93
00:08:13,431 --> 00:08:16,017
Won't you need to find another way
to make a living?

94
00:09:11,322 --> 00:09:12,948
He'll be 100 days old next month.

95
00:09:13,032 --> 00:09:15,201
It's not too late
to get out and come back.

96
00:09:15,284 --> 00:09:17,495
A dad should be able to look his kid
in the eyes.

97
00:09:36,389 --> 00:09:37,223
Hey.

98
00:09:38,599 --> 00:09:39,725
Is it even my kid?

99
00:09:41,102 --> 00:09:43,145
-What?
-If you need money, find someone else.

100
00:09:43,229 --> 00:09:45,064
Don't drag random people into it.

101
00:10:20,057 --> 00:10:21,100
Why not just take it?

102
00:10:22,643 --> 00:10:25,271
Take this money, and in return,

103
00:10:25,938 --> 00:10:27,523
I never want to see you two again.

104
00:10:28,482 --> 00:10:29,692
Don't worry.

105
00:10:30,609 --> 00:10:31,694
This is the last time.

106
00:10:34,780 --> 00:10:38,909
I just thought I should show the baby
his father's face at least once.

107
00:10:38,993 --> 00:10:41,912
I thought that was my duty as his mother.

108
00:10:48,252 --> 00:10:50,379
You should say your last goodbye.

109
00:11:24,830 --> 00:11:27,082
Where's the money, you punk?
You don't have any?

110
00:11:27,166 --> 00:11:28,417
Then you should get beaten.

111
00:11:40,513 --> 00:11:42,306
Living honestly gets you nowhere.

112
00:11:43,390 --> 00:11:45,184
If you can't give your kid anything,

113
00:11:45,851 --> 00:11:48,145
then your kid will grow up always losing.

114
00:11:49,271 --> 00:11:53,818
I didn't want to live like that,
so I chose to win, whatever the means.

115
00:11:55,152 --> 00:11:56,070
So…

116
00:11:59,490 --> 00:12:00,491
just take the money.

117
00:12:02,326 --> 00:12:03,160
No.

118
00:12:05,579 --> 00:12:06,413
You lost.

119
00:12:08,499 --> 00:12:09,834
There's something in this world

120
00:12:11,168 --> 00:12:13,045
that you can never win against.

121
00:12:15,548 --> 00:12:17,049
Even if I have to starve,

122
00:12:17,132 --> 00:12:19,218
I won't raise my baby with dirty money.

123
00:12:20,302 --> 00:12:21,345
I won't

124
00:12:22,596 --> 00:12:23,806
raise my baby like that.

125
00:13:04,763 --> 00:13:06,640
So I hope you'll prove it, sir.

126
00:13:07,474 --> 00:13:09,101
That you're different from him.

127
00:13:11,312 --> 00:13:13,063
I'll get us some drinks.

128
00:13:24,241 --> 00:13:26,535
Why did you bring me to the funeral home?

129
00:13:28,829 --> 00:13:30,122
Thinking of your own father?

130
00:13:36,128 --> 00:13:37,129
I never met him.

131
00:13:38,589 --> 00:13:40,883
He passed away before I was born.

132
00:13:46,055 --> 00:13:48,682
Not having any memories might be better.

133
00:13:53,646 --> 00:13:55,022
I've never met him,

134
00:13:55,564 --> 00:13:57,191
but I heard he was a good man.

135
00:13:59,526 --> 00:14:00,778
If he were alive,

136
00:14:02,279 --> 00:14:04,823
I think I would have liked him a lot.

137
00:14:06,533 --> 00:14:08,911
Even if he wasn't a good man,

138
00:14:09,703 --> 00:14:11,413
I would still have liked to meet him.

139
00:14:14,833 --> 00:14:16,126
Because he's my father.

140
00:14:36,230 --> 00:14:38,232
I don't know what you're trying to do,

141
00:14:38,732 --> 00:14:40,734
but don't make a scene
in front of Grandma.

142
00:14:41,568 --> 00:14:42,695
Let's take it outside.

143
00:14:45,030 --> 00:14:45,906
What a truly…

144
00:14:49,827 --> 00:14:51,453
cruel twist of fate,

145
00:14:52,454 --> 00:14:53,455
Jang Tae-ha.

146
00:15:15,811 --> 00:15:17,187
Baek Sang-gil!

147
00:15:41,462 --> 00:15:43,130
Don't run. Face the consequences.

148
00:16:00,981 --> 00:16:01,815
Consequences?

149
00:16:02,816 --> 00:16:04,860
It's a gift for taking off your gloves.

150
00:16:04,943 --> 00:16:07,738
From now on, get in fights
that reek of blood, not sweat.

151
00:16:09,490 --> 00:16:10,657
Tae-ha!

152
00:16:12,242 --> 00:16:15,746
Every day, your imagination will
eat away at you, wondering…

153
00:16:17,372 --> 00:16:19,291
about my plan for you.

154
00:16:32,387 --> 00:16:34,389
No. You lost.

155
00:16:35,682 --> 00:16:36,850
I won't

156
00:16:37,351 --> 00:16:38,769
raise my baby like that.

157
00:16:56,203 --> 00:16:57,579
Baek Sang-gil!

158
00:17:21,562 --> 00:17:22,688
No!

159
00:18:29,463 --> 00:18:30,714
Let's put…

160
00:18:34,843 --> 00:18:36,511
an end to this twisted fate of ours.

161
00:18:39,473 --> 00:18:40,307
No.

162
00:18:44,519 --> 00:18:46,438
No! You can't!

163
00:19:24,434 --> 00:19:29,606
You both always end a drinking session
with an order of gochujang stew.

164
00:19:36,780 --> 00:19:38,323
You like this too?

165
00:19:39,241 --> 00:19:40,075
Yes.

166
00:19:42,577 --> 00:19:44,371
You've got old-fashioned taste.

167
00:19:44,871 --> 00:19:46,123
It's good for hangovers.

168
00:21:10,999 --> 00:21:12,209
You're going to do what?

169
00:21:12,292 --> 00:21:15,754
A typhoon can carve out a path
where there was none.

170
00:21:15,837 --> 00:21:19,007
After our peaceful village
went through all that ruckus,

171
00:21:19,716 --> 00:21:23,470
I realized I can't just keep waiting
for my spiritual powers to return

172
00:21:23,553 --> 00:21:25,847
and that I should find a way
to make a living.

173
00:21:25,931 --> 00:21:27,015
So,

174
00:21:28,016 --> 00:21:29,476
you're learning tarot cards?

175
00:21:29,559 --> 00:21:33,939
These things are about as accurate
as a shaman's readings.

176
00:21:34,439 --> 00:21:37,317
All right, then. Give us a reading.

177
00:21:37,401 --> 00:21:40,278
Will there be another ruckus
in our village?

178
00:21:41,696 --> 00:21:43,532
Well, then. Shall I take a look?

179
00:21:43,615 --> 00:21:45,325
-Yeah.
-Okay.

180
00:21:45,409 --> 00:21:47,411
You have to shuffle these cards with care.

181
00:21:51,123 --> 00:21:52,416
All righty.

182
00:21:53,208 --> 00:21:54,042
Not bad.

183
00:21:54,126 --> 00:21:56,294
Let me see.

184
00:21:59,464 --> 00:22:01,049
I think it's this one.

185
00:22:09,641 --> 00:22:11,852
It says spring will come to many places.

186
00:22:19,067 --> 00:22:20,193
MUSCLE ACHES
BRUISES

187
00:22:20,277 --> 00:22:23,071
The bottom line is you got hurt saving me.

188
00:22:26,116 --> 00:22:27,492
Use this to treat it.

189
00:22:28,368 --> 00:22:29,369
I'll get going.

190
00:22:30,996 --> 00:22:32,998
I just couldn't figure it out.

191
00:22:34,958 --> 00:22:35,792
What?

192
00:22:35,876 --> 00:22:37,127
When I saw test papers,

193
00:22:38,420 --> 00:22:41,047
the answers would just pop into my head.

194
00:22:42,174 --> 00:22:45,260
But no matter how much
I looked into a woman's heart,

195
00:22:45,760 --> 00:22:46,845
I couldn't get it.

196
00:22:48,889 --> 00:22:53,643
You said you couldn't feel my sincerity,
but I had no idea what to do.

197
00:22:56,813 --> 00:22:58,732
To be honest, I still don't get it.

198
00:23:00,275 --> 00:23:03,695
If I were to just tell you
how I feel right now…

199
00:23:05,572 --> 00:23:07,324
I want to keep

200
00:23:08,575 --> 00:23:13,997
making memories with you,
like that time at the pub.

201
00:23:16,333 --> 00:23:17,667
Want some hangover soup?

202
00:23:25,800 --> 00:23:27,677
Go Eun-sae once said…

203
00:23:28,261 --> 00:23:30,305
Why get your memory back
if you believe him?

204
00:23:30,388 --> 00:23:32,015
How lonely must that be?

205
00:23:32,098 --> 00:23:35,936
Not being able to share the memories
you made with the person you love.

206
00:23:37,354 --> 00:23:39,731
Sharing the same memories

207
00:23:40,732 --> 00:23:43,860
means that you were
very close to each other.

208
00:23:45,153 --> 00:23:48,365
But since we were always bickering,
fighting over our pride,

209
00:23:48,949 --> 00:23:50,742
we couldn't share those moments.

210
00:23:52,244 --> 00:23:54,788
If I had amnesia too,

211
00:23:55,288 --> 00:23:57,791
I'd reset everything
and live my life anew.

212
00:23:59,084 --> 00:24:00,460
But I can't do that.

213
00:24:02,754 --> 00:24:03,630
So just…

214
00:24:09,094 --> 00:24:10,720
give me another chance.

215
00:24:18,895 --> 00:24:20,230
I know I look pathetic,

216
00:24:20,981 --> 00:24:24,943
saying we should break up
and then asking you to get back together.

217
00:24:27,070 --> 00:24:27,946
But

218
00:24:29,114 --> 00:24:30,865
I can't help still liking you.

219
00:24:42,627 --> 00:24:43,628
Hey.

220
00:24:44,212 --> 00:24:46,590
That's all you've got for your girlfriend?

221
00:24:49,175 --> 00:24:50,010
"Girlfriend"?

222
00:24:52,220 --> 00:24:54,598
Girlfriend… So are we…

223
00:24:55,181 --> 00:24:57,726
Then are we back…

224
00:25:14,659 --> 00:25:16,620
Come in for a second.

225
00:25:16,703 --> 00:25:18,997
What in the world is it
that you want to give me?

226
00:25:19,080 --> 00:25:19,956
Sit here.

227
00:25:21,041 --> 00:25:22,500
Are you giving me pocket money?

228
00:25:33,720 --> 00:25:34,554
These are…

229
00:25:34,638 --> 00:25:37,641
You used to love these. Do you remember?

230
00:25:44,064 --> 00:25:45,774
Let's see what our Tae-ha will pick.

231
00:25:45,857 --> 00:25:47,692
Let's grab one.

232
00:25:47,776 --> 00:25:49,152
Grab the gavel. Go on.

233
00:25:49,235 --> 00:25:50,862
Yes, that one. The doctor's…

234
00:25:52,238 --> 00:25:53,448
Come on.

235
00:25:55,533 --> 00:25:56,660
Dang it.

236
00:25:57,160 --> 00:25:59,371
Like mother, like son, I guess.

237
00:25:59,454 --> 00:26:01,414
A mom who's a boxing fan

238
00:26:01,498 --> 00:26:03,667
and puts boxing gloves
on the birthday table.

239
00:26:03,750 --> 00:26:06,169
And a son who grabs them right away.

240
00:26:06,670 --> 00:26:09,923
I guess Tae-ha will become a boxer
when he grows up.

241
00:26:10,006 --> 00:26:13,218
Picking gloves on his first birthday.
Maybe he'll make it to nationals.

242
00:26:13,301 --> 00:26:15,261
Well, aren't you Miss Glass-half-full.

243
00:26:15,345 --> 00:26:18,139
You see,
I believe in these sorts of things.

244
00:26:18,723 --> 00:26:20,684
That's why I named him "Tae-ha."

245
00:26:21,643 --> 00:26:24,312
No matter how much a big river meanders,

246
00:26:24,396 --> 00:26:28,191
it flows steadily
and eventually reaches the sea.

247
00:26:28,817 --> 00:26:33,321
I hope Tae-ha will live his life
so that he can one day go down the path

248
00:26:33,405 --> 00:26:35,573
he wants to go.

249
00:26:38,410 --> 00:26:39,244
Why not?

250
00:26:39,327 --> 00:26:41,996
Whatever our Tae-ha does,
it'll be good no matter what.

251
00:26:42,080 --> 00:26:44,833
Even when you were a baby,

252
00:26:44,916 --> 00:26:49,129
you were always so sure
of what you wanted to do.

253
00:26:50,004 --> 00:26:52,799
But you didn't get to live it out
because of me.

254
00:26:55,135 --> 00:26:57,554
When I meet your mom in the afterlife,

255
00:26:58,471 --> 00:27:00,807
I won't be able to face her.

256
00:27:01,516 --> 00:27:02,350
Grandma.

257
00:27:02,434 --> 00:27:07,522
So, can you do me a favor
and help me save face?

258
00:27:12,318 --> 00:27:14,654
Be happy, Tae-ha.

259
00:27:21,202 --> 00:27:22,954
From now on,

260
00:27:23,455 --> 00:27:26,040
don't let anyone interfere with your life.

261
00:27:26,124 --> 00:27:30,920
Just think about yourself and be happy.

262
00:27:33,047 --> 00:27:37,635
You've already been through
so many rough valleys,

263
00:27:37,719 --> 00:27:39,304
so from now on,

264
00:27:40,180 --> 00:27:41,890
go find your ocean.

265
00:27:42,766 --> 00:27:45,727
Go find your happiness, okay?

266
00:27:53,109 --> 00:27:53,943
That's my boy.

267
00:27:59,157 --> 00:28:00,492
Oh my…

268
00:28:13,046 --> 00:28:14,756
Oh, my baby.

269
00:28:17,634 --> 00:28:21,846
THE LATE JANG HYE-SU

270
00:28:25,433 --> 00:28:28,561
Hello, ma'am. My name is Go Eun-sae.

271
00:28:37,779 --> 00:28:39,030
Won't you introduce me?

272
00:28:45,286 --> 00:28:46,830
She's the woman I like.

273
00:28:56,881 --> 00:28:57,715
That's it?

274
00:29:00,468 --> 00:29:02,679
My mom knows everything,
even if I don't tell her.

275
00:29:18,486 --> 00:29:21,072
Did you really not have
anything else to say?

276
00:29:21,155 --> 00:29:23,867
"She's the woman I like"? That's it?

277
00:29:24,367 --> 00:29:25,702
Do I need to say more?

278
00:29:26,244 --> 00:29:28,162
You have so much to say about me.

279
00:29:28,246 --> 00:29:32,000
Like how I'm so pretty, I wouldn't look
out of place walking a red carpet.

280
00:29:32,083 --> 00:29:35,795
Or how I'm so talented that I became
a star prosecutor at a young age.

281
00:29:35,879 --> 00:29:40,550
Or how I'm the woman
you'd give your life for.

282
00:29:40,633 --> 00:29:43,428
Or how I'm the woman
you want to meet again in your next life.

283
00:29:44,220 --> 00:29:47,557
You're not cool at all. So uncool.

284
00:29:47,640 --> 00:29:49,475
Right, Blessing?

285
00:29:53,104 --> 00:29:54,230
What's this?

286
00:30:20,006 --> 00:30:22,175
Everyone says they want me to be happy.

287
00:30:26,512 --> 00:30:27,513
Now…

288
00:30:29,599 --> 00:30:30,850
I want to be happy too.

289
00:30:41,486 --> 00:30:42,695
But…

290
00:30:44,489 --> 00:30:46,074
my happiness is Go Eun-sae.

291
00:30:50,244 --> 00:30:51,955
I know I'm uncool,

292
00:30:53,581 --> 00:30:55,208
but I don't know what else to say.

293
00:30:59,712 --> 00:31:01,798
I have to be with you to be happy.

294
00:31:15,103 --> 00:31:15,937
Will you…

295
00:31:18,314 --> 00:31:19,315
marry me?

296
00:31:32,036 --> 00:31:33,913
I think I already answered.

297
00:31:37,250 --> 00:31:39,711
I said that even though
I got my memory back,

298
00:31:40,336 --> 00:31:42,797
I still like Jang Tae-ha.

299
00:31:59,981 --> 00:32:03,109
Who else would I marry if not Jang Tae-ha?

300
00:32:18,499 --> 00:32:19,625
I love you.

301
00:32:20,835 --> 00:32:21,836
I love you too.

302
00:32:40,354 --> 00:32:42,315
-So cute!
-Adorable!

303
00:32:42,398 --> 00:32:43,441
How sweet.

304
00:32:43,524 --> 00:32:45,151
Would you look at that!

305
00:32:46,652 --> 00:32:49,614
I told you,
that dog is better than people.

306
00:33:12,178 --> 00:33:13,221
How pretty.

307
00:33:19,685 --> 00:33:23,773
With this, these two have pledged
to be one forever.

308
00:33:30,571 --> 00:33:31,572
Next,

309
00:33:31,656 --> 00:33:36,077
we have a song to celebrate
the marriage of the bride and groom.

310
00:33:36,160 --> 00:33:39,705
Please welcome them
with a big round of applause.

311
00:33:39,789 --> 00:33:41,332
The fairies of our village.

312
00:33:41,415 --> 00:33:44,168
A song
from Taffy Village's very own S.E.S!

313
00:34:14,323 --> 00:34:15,700
What's he doing?

314
00:34:21,914 --> 00:34:22,957
That's it!

315
00:34:24,500 --> 00:34:28,087
Why won't you tell me
Things that have already passed

316
00:34:28,171 --> 00:34:29,463
You look great!

317
00:34:29,547 --> 00:34:31,424
A cliché-filled old love story

318
00:34:33,968 --> 00:34:36,220
Tell me honestly

319
00:34:36,304 --> 00:34:42,185
But to me, you're the only one

320
00:34:43,352 --> 00:34:45,396
Don't be afraid

321
00:34:45,479 --> 00:34:47,982
I'm by your side

322
00:34:48,065 --> 00:34:52,195
To the end of our lives

323
00:34:52,278 --> 00:34:55,740
I hope you trust me

324
00:34:55,823 --> 00:34:57,909
Stay with me

325
00:35:01,245 --> 00:35:05,499
I'm becoming more like you

326
00:35:05,583 --> 00:35:07,710
Watch over me

327
00:35:14,634 --> 00:35:16,344
Bride, you can throw the bouquet now.

328
00:35:18,346 --> 00:35:20,139
One, two, three!

329
00:35:27,480 --> 00:35:28,648
What the…

330
00:35:28,731 --> 00:35:29,857
-Oh my.
-What happened?

331
00:35:29,941 --> 00:35:30,900
What should we do?

332
00:35:30,983 --> 00:35:32,360
-Throw it again.
-Here.

333
00:35:34,362 --> 00:35:35,529
-It's Su-ji!
-Yeah.

334
00:35:35,613 --> 00:35:36,948
No takebacks now.

335
00:35:39,659 --> 00:35:41,035
What's he doing?

336
00:35:42,078 --> 00:35:44,330
-Here.
-What's with him?

337
00:35:44,956 --> 00:35:46,916
He gave her flowers.

338
00:35:48,668 --> 00:35:50,586
What's going on with those two?

339
00:35:53,589 --> 00:35:56,092
-Love is in the air!
-Did he just cut those flowers?

340
00:35:56,676 --> 00:35:57,760
Get married!

341
00:35:57,843 --> 00:35:59,136
Accept his love!

342
00:36:01,013 --> 00:36:03,307
-What the…
-What?

343
00:36:09,272 --> 00:36:11,023
It's raining!

344
00:36:11,107 --> 00:36:13,192
Where do we go? Where?

345
00:36:13,693 --> 00:36:16,612
It's a sun-shower! Maybe a tiger
is getting married today too!

346
00:36:17,571 --> 00:36:18,823
-Right?
-Come here!

347
00:36:18,906 --> 00:36:21,409
Tae-ha, Eun-sae, come here. Hurry!

348
00:36:21,492 --> 00:36:22,535
Come on!

349
00:36:22,618 --> 00:36:24,787
-You're getting wet!
-Get in here!

350
00:36:25,997 --> 00:36:28,374
Man, what will we do?

351
00:36:29,417 --> 00:36:30,418
Goodness.

352
00:36:41,137 --> 00:36:44,807
For whatever reason, it always rained
on the hardest days of my life.

353
00:36:46,225 --> 00:36:48,019
In my bleakest moments,

354
00:36:48,519 --> 00:36:52,231
there was nothing
to shield me from the rain.

355
00:36:52,732 --> 00:36:55,026
It felt like a reminder
of how hopeless things were.

356
00:36:55,526 --> 00:36:56,694
So I don't like rain.

357
00:36:58,738 --> 00:37:00,489
Let's weather it together from now on.

358
00:37:02,325 --> 00:37:04,327
I'll be with you.

359
00:37:24,138 --> 00:37:26,432
-What are they doing?
-Why are they out in the rain?

360
00:37:26,515 --> 00:37:28,225
Come over here!

361
00:37:28,309 --> 00:37:30,603
I guess this will be another memory.

362
00:37:30,686 --> 00:37:32,313
Let's just play in the rain!

363
00:37:43,240 --> 00:37:44,116
Let's join them.

364
00:37:44,200 --> 00:37:46,369
Screw it. Let's go!

365
00:39:56,415 --> 00:39:59,793
We can't go on a honeymoon
because there are so many trials lined up,

366
00:39:59,877 --> 00:40:03,088
but we should at least
make it feel like our wedding night.

367
00:40:03,589 --> 00:40:04,423
Ta-da!

368
00:40:05,007 --> 00:40:07,801
They say it's a miracle remedy
that makes you young and firm.

369
00:40:08,302 --> 00:40:11,889
This is lion's mane liquor.

370
00:40:11,972 --> 00:40:13,599
It's super precious.

371
00:40:16,560 --> 00:40:17,853
This…

372
00:40:18,395 --> 00:40:20,523
How long has this been here?

373
00:40:21,023 --> 00:40:22,483
-It's a secret.
-A secret?

374
00:40:22,566 --> 00:40:23,609
Cheers!

375
00:40:34,495 --> 00:40:37,915
Shall we go do what we need to do now?

376
00:40:39,291 --> 00:40:40,125
Yeah.

377
00:40:44,213 --> 00:40:45,256
Let's go.

378
00:40:47,091 --> 00:40:47,967
Go Eun…

379
00:40:51,762 --> 00:40:52,596
shway.

380
00:40:59,186 --> 00:41:02,439
I re… really…

381
00:41:02,523 --> 00:41:03,399
Yeah?

382
00:41:08,112 --> 00:41:09,321
I really

383
00:41:09,822 --> 00:41:10,739
like

384
00:41:11,699 --> 00:41:12,741
Go Eun-sae.

385
00:41:15,536 --> 00:41:19,456
She said it was meant to make you younger,
but how much younger did you get?

386
00:41:19,540 --> 00:41:20,874
-Babe.
-Yeah?

387
00:41:20,958 --> 00:41:23,752
What am I supposed to do with a baby?

388
00:41:24,753 --> 00:41:25,879
I'm happy.

389
00:41:26,672 --> 00:41:27,548
So happy.

390
00:41:32,886 --> 00:41:34,555
-Babe?
-Yeah?

391
00:41:34,638 --> 00:41:36,265
Now's not the time to pass out.

392
00:41:36,348 --> 00:41:38,517
Get up. Babe.

393
00:41:38,601 --> 00:41:39,643
Oppa.

394
00:41:41,520 --> 00:41:45,566
-Yeah?
-Oppa.

395
00:41:49,570 --> 00:41:50,654
Jang Tae-ha.

396
00:41:53,616 --> 00:41:55,034
Mr. Jang Tae-ha!

397
00:41:55,534 --> 00:41:57,077
I'm so happy.

398
00:42:09,965 --> 00:42:10,883
Water…

399
00:42:11,383 --> 00:42:12,301
Water.

400
00:42:24,188 --> 00:42:25,189
Did you…

401
00:42:26,774 --> 00:42:27,733
Did you sleep well?

402
00:42:30,194 --> 00:42:33,530
What do you think?
When you let our one and only first night

403
00:42:33,614 --> 00:42:34,990
go to waste like that?

404
00:42:35,491 --> 00:42:38,243
How come I've never seen you
get drunk until now,

405
00:42:38,327 --> 00:42:41,705
and you pass out on our first night?
On our important wedding night?

406
00:42:47,544 --> 00:42:49,546
Does it… have to be at night?

407
00:42:52,132 --> 00:42:53,092
Can't it be

408
00:42:53,759 --> 00:42:56,345
our first morning too?

409
00:43:02,476 --> 00:43:06,146
Babe! What are you doing?

410
00:43:07,940 --> 00:43:09,983
Everyone's life has a genre.

411
00:43:10,484 --> 00:43:13,821
Ms. Min Su-ji and I are planning
to get married.

412
00:43:25,874 --> 00:43:27,459
At times, romance.

413
00:43:31,588 --> 00:43:33,549
-Dig deeper.
-You got it.

414
00:43:34,842 --> 00:43:36,218
At times, film noir.

415
00:43:38,387 --> 00:43:41,598
If we don't bury it deep,
the kimchi won't taste good. So dig deep.

416
00:43:41,682 --> 00:43:42,599
Yes.

417
00:43:43,100 --> 00:43:43,934
My back.

418
00:43:52,401 --> 00:43:54,319
Are you okay, sir?

419
00:43:56,530 --> 00:43:58,407
You absolute piece of filth!

420
00:43:58,490 --> 00:44:00,701
-No, Jeong-hwa. I'm okay.
-Look at this bastard!

421
00:44:00,784 --> 00:44:02,161
I'm okay.

422
00:44:02,244 --> 00:44:03,287
Hey, you bastard!

423
00:44:03,370 --> 00:44:04,496
I said I'm okay!

424
00:44:04,580 --> 00:44:05,539
I'm sorry!

425
00:44:05,622 --> 00:44:07,249
Dig deep! Deeper!

426
00:44:12,588 --> 00:44:14,256
At times, horror.

427
00:44:18,927 --> 00:44:21,263
You don't have a middle ground, do you?

428
00:44:21,346 --> 00:44:22,848
RANK: 82/82

429
00:44:29,396 --> 00:44:30,522
I hear it.

430
00:44:31,231 --> 00:44:32,274
I can hear it.

431
00:44:32,357 --> 00:44:34,943
I can hear the revered spirit.

432
00:44:35,027 --> 00:44:36,278
What?

433
00:44:45,579 --> 00:44:48,415
The revered spirit has returned!

434
00:44:49,583 --> 00:44:50,417
The heck?

435
00:44:51,585 --> 00:44:53,378
Revered spirit!

436
00:44:54,379 --> 00:44:56,715
Revered spirit, you have returned!

437
00:44:56,799 --> 00:44:58,717
You don't know how long I've waited!

438
00:44:58,801 --> 00:45:01,178
And at times, fantasy.

439
00:45:16,360 --> 00:45:17,778
Adding more photos again?

440
00:45:17,861 --> 00:45:20,739
Yeah, we should
stay on top of organizing them.

441
00:45:21,448 --> 00:45:23,200
You really love taking photos.

442
00:45:23,784 --> 00:45:25,953
After losing my memory,

443
00:45:26,036 --> 00:45:28,330
I realized that these are like
emergency funds.

444
00:45:29,915 --> 00:45:33,126
When I'm having a hard time,
when I'm exhausted,

445
00:45:33,627 --> 00:45:35,087
when I don't know where to go…

446
00:45:35,963 --> 00:45:39,716
These are like emergency funds
you can dip into during tough times.

447
00:45:43,428 --> 00:45:45,889
Though the genre may change unpredictably,

448
00:45:45,973 --> 00:45:49,643
you share every scene with people
who stand by your side.

449
00:45:50,352 --> 00:45:53,313
And the memories you make with them
come together, frame by frame,

450
00:45:53,897 --> 00:45:56,275
to complete the drama we call life.

451
00:45:58,318 --> 00:46:03,115
Perhaps living is all about remembering
the scenes that have passed.

452
00:46:09,413 --> 00:46:11,039
Say hello. They're from this village.

453
00:46:14,334 --> 00:46:15,168
Stop right there.

454
00:46:16,128 --> 00:46:17,296
Eun-sae's here.

455
00:46:22,134 --> 00:46:23,802
Happy birthday to you…

456
00:46:23,886 --> 00:46:26,597
If I leave something like this behind,

457
00:46:26,680 --> 00:46:29,766
even if I happen to lose my memory again,

458
00:46:30,267 --> 00:46:33,228
I think I'd be able to believe

459
00:46:33,312 --> 00:46:36,940
that I lived a happy life
with my loved ones.

460
00:46:41,612 --> 00:46:42,946
No need to worry.

461
00:46:43,447 --> 00:46:45,407
I can just tell you everything.

462
00:46:47,576 --> 00:46:48,744
You're right.

463
00:46:50,203 --> 00:46:53,248
Now I have someone who will remember
every moment of my life.

464
00:47:00,547 --> 00:47:01,965
You must like taking pictures.

465
00:47:02,049 --> 00:47:04,009
I've been taking pictures
since I was a kid.

466
00:47:04,509 --> 00:47:08,305
If I had a mom and dad, they would have
taken pictures of me growing up.

467
00:47:08,388 --> 00:47:11,391
They would have remembered
and told me about it later.

468
00:47:12,309 --> 00:47:16,313
Someone like me can't reminisce about
the past unless I leave something behind.

469
00:47:17,856 --> 00:47:21,443
So this is what it feels like
to have family.

470
00:47:37,042 --> 00:47:38,919
Should we capture this moment too?

471
00:47:40,796 --> 00:47:41,755
Should we?

472
00:47:44,216 --> 00:47:45,842
Three, two…

473
00:47:46,343 --> 00:47:48,345
-Wait.
-Blessing, you want in too?

474
00:47:48,428 --> 00:47:50,847
Look at the camera. Three, two, one.

475
00:47:56,645 --> 00:47:57,938
It came out great.

476
00:48:01,817 --> 00:48:03,360
-It's pretty.
-Yeah.

477
00:48:16,081 --> 00:48:18,625
-I should put this in the album too.
-Right now?

478
00:48:18,709 --> 00:48:19,668
A little later.

479
00:49:48,423 --> 00:49:52,719
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi

